  "caption": "Flashback to teen Quinn: soccer three days a week, basketball the rest, and then a sore bump just below the knee that hated running, jumping, kneeling and stairs.\n\nThat's often Osgood-Schlatter, where repeated pull from the tendon irritates a growing area below the knee. It often settles with growth, though it can linger, and the bump usually stays. Rest alone tends not to sort it out.\n\nWhat can help: reducing the sport dose rather than stopping, the next-morning rule (soreness settled by the next day and not building week to week), progressive knee and hip strength, and dropping one overlapping commitment.\n\nGet it checked if there's night pain, fever, a hot swollen joint, locking, or pain away from the bump.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
